{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Elohim spoke to Moses.</b> He spoke with him in reproof, because he made it difficult to speak and to say, ״Why have you done evil to this people?״" "<b>And He said to him: I am YHWH.</b> Trustworthy to pay good reward to those who walk before Me — and not for nothing did I send you, but to fulfill My word that I spoke to the forefathers, the first ones. And in this expression we find that it is expounded in several places: ״I am YHWH״ — trustworthy to exact punishment, when it is said in connection with punishment — as in ״וְחִלַּלְתָּ אֶת שֵׁם אֱלֹהֶיךָ אֲנִי ה׳״ (Leviticus 19:12); and when it is said in connection with the fulfillment of commandments — as in ״וּשְׁמַרְתֶּם מִצְוֹתַי וַעֲשִׂיתֶם אֹתָם אֲנִי ה׳״ (ibid. 22) — trustworthy to give reward."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:50:44.904745298Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}